{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1087", "sample_idx": 30, "model_name": "meta/llama-3.3-70b-instruct", "content": "the social network is a movie that tells the story of the founding of facebook and the subsequent lawsuits that followed. the film is directed by david fincher and written by aaron sorkin, based on the book \"the accidental billionaires\" by ben mezrich.\n\nthe movie starts with mark zuckerberg, played by jesse eisenberg, as a harvard undergraduate who is trying to find his place in the world. he is a computer genius and a social outcast, and he finds solace in his computer programming skills. after a bitter breakup with his girlfriend, erica, mark creates a website called \"facemash\" which becomes a huge hit on campus.\n\nthe success of facemash catches the attention of the winklevoss twins, cameron and tyler, who approach mark with an idea for a social networking site exclusively for harvard students. mark agrees to work on the project, but he soon becomes obsessed with the idea and starts working on his own version of the site, which eventually becomes facebook.\n\nas facebook gains popularity, mark becomes increasingly distant from his friends and acquaintances, including his best friend eduardo saverin, played by andrew garfield. eduardo is a business major who helps mark launch facebook, but their friendship is strained as mark's priorities shift from their friendship to the success of the site.\n\nthe movie also explores the theme of class and privilege, as mark and his friends navigate the complexities of harvard's social hierarchy. the film portrays mark as a brilliant but awkward and sometimes ruthless individual who is willing to do whatever it takes to succeed.\n\nthe acting in the movie is superb, with jesse eisenberg delivering a nuanced and complex performance as mark zuckerberg. andrew garfield is also excellent as eduardo saverin, and justin timberlake is convincing as sean parker, the co-founder of napster who becomes a key player 